<TMU|<tuple|1.1.0|2025.0.15>>

<style|<tuple|generic|number-europe>>

<\body>
  <doc-data|<doc-title|Huffman Coding>|<doc-author|<author-data|<author-name|Jason Freddie>>>>

  Consider we are facing a character-coding problem, we have some char to be restored:

  <\big-table|<block|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|>|<cell|a>|<cell|b>|<cell|c>|<cell|d>|<cell|e>|<cell|f>>|<row|<cell|Frequency(in thousands)>|<cell|45>|<cell|13>|<cell|12>|<cell|16>|<cell|9>|<cell|5>>|<row|<cell|Fixed-length codeword>|<cell|000>|<cell|001>|<cell|010>|<cell|011>|<cell|100>|<cell|101>>|<row|<cell|Variable-length codeword>|<cell|0>|<cell|101>|<cell|100>|<cell|111>|<cell|1101>|<cell|1100>>>>>>
    \;
  </big-table>

  In Fixed-length codeword, we will use <math|(45+...+5)*\<times\>3\<times\>*1000=300,000> bits,

  but for Variable-length codeword, we have only <math|<around*|(|45\<times\>1+<around*|(|13+12+16|)>\<times\>3+<around*|(|9+5|)>\<times\>4|)>\<times\>1000=224000> bits.

  Or more math, low frequency times high length get the minimum result, which is rearrangement ineq. .

  Also, the coding we will use is prefix codes, which means no codeword is other's prefix.

  We can formulate the problem of codeword to set the min of:

  <\equation>
    <below|min |Tree>B<around*|(|Tree|)>=<below|min|Tree><below|<big|sum>|c\<in\>C>freq<around*|(|c|)>\<ast\>d<rsub|Tree><around*|(|c|)>,
  </equation>

  where in our last table <math|C=<around*|{|a,b,c,d,e,f|}>,d<rsub|T> ><math|is the depth of char in certain tree>.

  Why building in a tree? Actually, tree height is a perfect approximation of entropy.

  \;

  <section|Shannon's Source Coding Theorem and Entropy>

  At this part, we will show that the Shannon's entropy is the best way to do codeword.

  Firstly, base on the simple observation, we have the following ineq. to show why we need prefix codes.

  <\theorem>
    (Kraft's ineq.)Set <math|f:c\<rightarrow\>f<around*|(|c|)>\<in\><around*|{|0,1|}><rsup|\<ast\>>> which makes a coding way for c.And <math|l:<around*|{|0,1|}><rsup|\<ast\>>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-Z\><rsup|+>.>Any prefix code f we have the ineq.

    <\equation>
      <below|<big|sum>|c\<in\>C>2<rsup|-l<around*|(|f<around*|(|c|)>|)>>\<leqslant\>1.
    </equation>
  </theorem>

  Proof is on wiki and quite long.

  Arrange <math|C=<around*|{|c<rsub|i>|}><rsub|i=1><rsup|n>,l\<circ\>f<around*|(|c<rsub|i>|)>\<assign\>l<rsub|i>>,then we want to solve the optimization problem:

  <\equation>
    <below|<below|min|l<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,l<rsub|n>\<in\>\<bbb-Z\><rsup|+>><below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>l<rsub|i >p<rsub|i>,|s.t.<below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>2<rsup|-l<rsub|i>>\<leqslant\>1.>
  </equation>

  we don't need to strenghthen that <math|p<rsub|i>=<frac|freq<around*|(|c<rsub|i>|)>|<below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>freq<around*|(|c<rsub|i>|)>>>.Next, since <math|<below|min|l<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,l<rsub|n>\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|>><below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>l<rsub|i>p<rsub|i>\<leqslant\><below|min|l<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,l<rsub|n>\<in\>\<bbb-Z\><rsup|+>><below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>l<rsub|i>p<rsub|i>><math|>,

  we will change to solve:

  <\equation>
    <below|<below|min|l<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,l<rsub|n>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>><below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>l<rsub|i >p<rsub|i>,|s.t.<below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>2<rsup|-l<rsub|i>>\<leqslant\>1.>
  </equation>

  This is the common relaxation of integer optimization problem.

  Firstly, set <math|<below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>2<rsup|-l<rsub|i>>\<less\>1,>which is in the interior of feasible set. Then <math|l<rsub|i>\<gtr\>0 \<forall\>i>,for if <math|\<exists\>i<rsup|\<ast\>> s.t. l<rsub|i<rsup|*\<ast\>>>\<leqslant\>0\<Rightarrow\>>

  <math|2<rsup|-l<rsub|i<rsup|\<ast\>>>>\<gtr\>1>, contradict to <math|<below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>2<rsup|-l<rsub|i>>\<less\>1>.

  Next, set <math|<around*|{|l<rsub|i><rsup|\<ast\>>|}> i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>> to be solution. Since <math|l<rsub|i>\<gtr\>0 \<forall\>i,>you can choose <math|l<rsub|i><rsup|\<ast\>>\<gtr\>l<rsub|i><rsup|\<ast\>\<ast\>>\<gtr\>0\<Rightarrow\><below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>l<rsub|i><rsup|\<ast\>\<ast\>>p<rsub|i>\<less\><below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>l<rsub|i><rsup|\<ast\>>p<rsub|i>>,

  contradict to <math|<around*|{|l<rsub|i><rsup|\<ast\>>|}> i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>> is a solution. So we can not choose <math|l<rsub|i>> from the interior,then the optimiztion problem changes to:

  <\equation>
    <below|<below|min|l<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,l<rsub|n>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>><below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>l<rsub|i >p<rsub|i>,|s.t.<below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>2<rsup|-l<rsub|i>>=1.>
  </equation>

  It is much more simple, set <math|q<rsub|i>\<assign\>2<rsup|-l<rsub|i>>,L<around*|(|l;\<lambda\>|)>=<below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>><rsub| >p<rsub|i> log<around*|(|<frac|1|q<rsub|i>>|)>+\<lambda\><around*|(|<below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>q<rsub|i>-1|)>\<Rightarrow\>q<rsub|i>=p<rsub|i>\<Rightarrow\>l<rsub|i>=log<rsub|2><around*|(|<frac|1|p<rsub|i>>|)>.>

  \;

  Then we get the Shannon's entropy.

  \;

  <section| From Entropy to Huffman coding>

  Set <math|H<around*|(|p|)>\<assign\><below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>p<rsub|i>log<rsub|2><around*|(|<frac|1|p<rsub|i>>|)>>.<math|H:\<Delta\><rsup|n>\<rightarrow\>\<bbb-R\>.> Since <math|<below|min|l\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsup|n>>\<leqslant\><below|min|l\<in\>\<bbb-N\><rsup|n>>>:

  <\equation>
    H<around*|(|p|)>\<leqslant\><below|<big|sum>|i\<in\><around*|[|n|]>>p<rsub|i>d<rsub|T><around*|(|c<rsub|i>|)>\<leqslant\>H<around*|(|p|)>+1.
  </equation>

  In this way,building a binary tree is a good approximation to Shannon's entropy and it can prove before that in this way the value of codeword is no bigger than 1 compares to Shannon's entropy.

  \;

  \;
